  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "6.7.8.3, client-only fixes against Firefly III API 6.7.8, checked against a live 6.7.9. GetConfiguration no longer fails: ConfigValueFilter gains the seven configuration.* settings the server returns and the spec lists only for updates, or not at all (enable_exchange_rates, use_running_balance, enable_external_map, enable_external_rates, allow_webhooks, enable_batch_processing, valid_url_protocols), and reads an unrecognised title as Unknown instead of failing the whole list. The README now lists what the server clears on null and what needs another value: a split's foreign amount goes with \"0\", a bill's group with \"\", a credit card's payment date only with a role change; a bill's end and extension dates and a piggy bank's group cannot be removed. An update of a group with several splits needs GroupTitle. 6.7.8.2: ClearedFields.Clear (update.Clear(u => u.TargetDate)) sends a field as null so the server removes it; BillUpdate.EndDate and ExtensionDate are DateTime?; RuleTriggerUpdate gains Prohibited, which the spec leaves out. 6.7.8.1: requests send only what the caller set; the bool/int fields of the *Update models are bool?/int?; *Store active defaults to true; piggy banks send account_id and a currency; responses read numbers as strings, date-times as dates and a null budget CurrencyDecimalPlaces; CategoryUpdate.Notes and Color are three-state.",
